b2=0.1) against the SFT checkpoint as reference.\n\n3) FIXED-ACROSS-ARMS CONTROLS (the whole experiment is the factor \"game adversarially\")\n- Base model: Llama-2-7B-chat, identical HF checkpoint across arms.\n- Teacher data volume: token-matched per arm (total SFT tokens equal to \u00b10.5%).\n- Self-play volume: 50k episodes/arm; decoding identical (rollout temp 0.7, top-p 0.95; greedy 0 for eval).\n- DPO hyperparameters identical (\u03b2, LR, epochs, batch, seq len).\n- Seeds: same seed set reused across arms so \u0394s are paired per seed {0..4}.\n- Eval protocol and prompt templates identical; same held-out benchmark splits; same frozen opponent pool for in-game eval.\n\n4) COMMITTED HYPERPARAMETERS (design commitments, not SPAG-verified)\n- Model: Llama-2-7B-chat (HF), full-parameter fine-tuning via FSDP/DeepSpeed stage-2.\n- SFT: 3 epochs, AdamW, LR 2e-5, cosine schedule, warmup 3%, batch 64, max_seq_len 2048, weight decay 0.1.\n- Teacher data: 1,000 GPT-4 games/arm/seed \u2192 ~60k SFT examples \u2248 ~1.5M tokens/arm (token-matched).\n- Self-play: 50k episodes/arm, temperature 1.0 partner / 0.7 self, episode = \u22651 and \u22648 role-turn pairs or target hit, clue \u226430 tokens, guess \u226410 tokens.\n- DPO: \u03b2=0.1, LR 5e-6, 1 epoch, batch 32, seq 2048, reference = SFT ckpt.\n- Taboo config (assumption): target word + 2\u20133 taboo words; clue must not contain target/taboo words or subwords; hit = guesser names target within budget.\n- Eval: GSM8K 8-shot CoT, StrategyQA CoT, HotpotQA (distractor) 2-shot, ASDiv CoT, last-letter & coin-flip few-shot symbolic; greedy, exact-match/pass@1.\n\n5) EVALUATION\n- Pre: base model on all benchmarks. Post: each arm\u00d7seed on the same splits with same prompts.\n- Primary metric per arm: distribution over seeds of \u0394 = post_mean \u2212 pre_mean on a benchmark aggregate (averaged over the six tasks) AND benchmark-wise \u0394s (reported separately so transfer breadth is visible, never cherry-picked).\n- Secondary: Taboo win-rate vs a FROZEN opponent pool (5 fixed Llama-2-7B GPT-4-distilled Taboo players, fixed decoding), 100 held-out Taboo instances \u00d7 5 opponents, win-rate per seeded arm (A/B/C only; descriptive, Section 0).\n\n6) ANALYSIS PLAN (per-seed paired, nonparametric)\n- Per seed s: \u0394_{arm,s}. All contrasts are paired on the same seed set.\n- Primary contrasts, declared a priori: H1: \u0394_A > \u0394_B; H2: \u0394_A > \u0394_C. Test: one-sided exact permutation/Wilcoxon signed-rank on per-seed \u0394 pairs; Holm-Bonferroni correction across H1,H2 (\u03b1 = 0.05).\n- Report: mean \u0394, SD, 95% CI via seed-resampled bootstrap, and Hedges' g for A-vs-B and A-vs-C (with CIs). Interpret only when H1\u2227H2 pass with g CI excluding 0.\n- Supporting (pre-registered as conditional, not primary): A vs D (self-play ablation) and A vs E (data-volume control) \u2014 if either fails, the headline claim is weakened accordingly.\n- Diagnostics: self-play win-rate trajectory should plateau (monitor for collapse/cheating); rollout perplexity/diversity tracked; benchmark contamination check = no benchmark train or few-shot exemplar text appears in any training data.\n\n7) FEASIBILITY / GPU-BUDGET NOTE (for a peer with compute; nothing runs here)\n- Bottleneck is self-play rollouts: 50k episodes \u00d7 2 actors per arm \u2248 100k generation calls/arm. vLLM on 8\u00d7A100-80GB \u2248 1\u20132 days/arm.\n- SFT: ~2\u20134 h/run on 8\u00d7A100-80GB (or 8\u00d7A100-40GB); DPO ~3\u20136 h/run.\n- Total runs: A/B/C = 15 (SFT+SP+DPO), D = 3 (SFT only), E = 3 (SFT only) \u2192 \u2248 2\u20133 weeks wall-clock on 8\u00d7A100-80GB, or ~$5\u20139k cloud (A100-80GB at ~$2/h). GPT-4 API cost for teacher demos is minor (~$200). All data components are public/open: Llama-2 (HF), GSM8K/StrategyQA/HotpotQA/ASDiv (HF), Taboo wordlists (open sources such as Hugging Face Taboo sets), so the plan is runnable by an unaffiliated peer.\n\n8) ASSUMPTIONS vs FIXED REQUIREMENTS\nFixed tas